# Known (prometheus#8312, closed), with a new cause (RESULTS.md, finding 2): the wall clock goes
# back 5 minutes before step 20. The scrape loops of the agent and of the server then stamp
# every scrape with the last aligned time before the step, until the clock is there again: 199 of
# 240 pairs of scrapes a second apart carry one timestamp (the check `times`). The server drops
# 81,585 of its own scraped samples as duplicates of a timestamp, although its out-of-order
# window of 10 minutes covers the step. With --no-scrape.adjust-timestamps (--set
# adjust=--no-scrape.adjust-timestamps) every scrape has its own timestamp. The verdict line
# names finding 1 first; the run's result.json has the `times` finding too.
# expect: violation      (change to ok when the bug is fixed)
disk=none | run T=20:-300
